# p7zip

p7zip is a port of the Windows programs 7z.exe and 7za.exe provided by 7-zip, the file archiver with the highest compression ratio.

- Homepage: http://p7zip.sourceforge.net/
- 7-zip Homepage: www.7-zip.org

## Components

- **7z**: Uses plugins (7z.so and Codecs/Rar29.so) to handle archives
- **7za**: A stand-alone executable with support for fewer archive formats
- **7zr**: A light stand-alone executable supporting only 7z/LZMA/BCJ/BCJ2
- **7zG**: A GUI version (see GUI/readme.txt)

## Important Notes

### Backup on Linux/Unix
⚠️ **CAUTION**: Do not use the 7-zip format for backup purposes on Linux/Unix because it does not store the owner/group of files.

For backing up directories on Linux/Unix:
```bash
# Backup
tar cf - directory | 7za a -si directory.tar.7z

# Restore
7za x -so directory.tar.7z | tar xf -
```

### File Sharing
For sharing files across Unix/MacOS/Windows:
```bash
7za a directory.7z directory
```
**Note**: 
- Avoid using "-r" flag as it may not work as expected
- Don't use directory/* as it won't match hidden files (e.g., .profile)

## Building from Source

### Prerequisites
Choose the appropriate makefile for your OS:
- makefile.linux
- makefile.freebsd
- makefile.cygwin
Copy it to `makefile.machine`

### Build Commands

| Command         | Description                                                                 |
|-----------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| make clean      | Cleans all directories                                                     |
| make            | Builds bin/7za                                                            |
| make sfx        | Builds bin/7zCon.sfx (for SFX archives)                                   |
| make 7z         | Builds bin/7z and plugins                                                  |
| make 7zr        | Builds bin/7zr                                                            |
| make all        | Builds bin/7za and bin/7zCon.sfx                                          |
| make all2       | Builds 7za, 7z (with plugins), and 7zCon.sfx                              |
| make all3       | Builds all components including 7zr                                        |
| make test       | Tests bin/7za                                                             |
| make test_7z    | Tests bin/7z                                                              |
| make test_7zr   | Tests bin/7zr                                                             |

### CMAKE Build
For building 7za only:
1. Navigate to CPP/7zip/CMAKE
2. Edit generate.sh for your target
3. Run ./generate.sh
4. Build using make or your IDE

## Installation

### Method 1: Using install script
1. Edit install.sh to set DEST_HOME
2. Run ./install.sh (requires root for /usr/local)

### Method 2: Manual installation
- For 7za: Copy bin/7za to desired location
- For 7z: Copy 7z, 7z.so, and Codecs directory together
- For SFX: Copy bin/7zCon.sfx to the same directory as 7za/7z

## Usage

Basic commands (use 7z or 7za):
```bash
# Test archive
7za t archive.7z

# List contents
7za l archive.7z

# Extract files
7za x archive.7z

# Create archive
7za a archive.7z file1 fileN

# Create SFX archive
7za a -sfx archive.exe dir1

# Password protection
7za a -pmy_password archive.7z dir1

# Archive with header encryption (.7z only)
7za a -mhe=on -pmy_password archive.7z dir1
```

### Supported Formats
```bash
# ZIP archives
7za a -tzip archive.zip files

# TAR archives
7za a -ttar archive.tar files

# GZIP compression
7za a -tgzip file.gz file

# BZIP2 compression
7za a -tbzip2 archive.bz2 file
```

## Limitations

### General
- No uid/gid support for .tar format

### Unix-specific
- UNICODE filenames require UTF-8 environment
  - Set: `export LANG=en_US.UTF-8 ; unset LC_CTYPE`
  - Use `-no-utf16` flag for local-only archives
- Windows file permissions are ignored

